# Transport layer II.f: certificate transport (ATLAS-II)

* `isLorentzian_pullback`: `Jᵀ H J` is Lorentzian when `H` is (frame `K E`).
* `VacuumCertificate.transport`: a vacuum certificate for `(h, hi)` on `V` and a coordinate change
  `Φ : U → V` with genuine Jacobian `J`, right inverse `K`, pull-back data `G = Jᵀ H(Φ) J`,
  `GI = K HI(Φ) Kᵀ` on a nonempty open `U` give a vacuum certificate for `(g, gi)` on `U`. Each field
  is discharged separately; the Ricci field is the transformation law `ricciOf_transform` applied to
  `ricciOf h hi = 0`.
* `VacuumCertificate.transport_of_relation`: the same from the first-release bundle
  `CoordRelation g h U V Φ Ψ J` (4D), an explicit right inverse `K` of `J` on `U`, `IsOpen U`,
  `U.Nonempty`, and **any** genuine left inverse `gi` of `g` on `U` (it is then automatically the
  transported inverse, by uniqueness of inverses).

`CoordRelation` has no openness/nonemptiness fields; they are explicit hypotheses here.
